13"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T12:05:32-08:00","id":1498693,"title":"","content":"So, for clarity's sake, The Circle of the Crone sourcebook from 1e has philosophical roles as a broad structural element that might be used across the various cults of the Circle which, when used, basically lays out just how far in a vampire has gone. The Virgin (and the Fool, the masculine counterpart) are those who have not killed yet, which broadly marks them as the youths at the table. There's a notable exception, though, if you have gone an exceptionally long time having never killed anyone, at which point the kiddies instead have the designation of being wise and skilled enough to have not done that, and thus they earn the philosophical rank of Maiden and Trickster.<br /> <br /> As for how one does it, I find the question answers itself. You don't fucking kill anyone. It' simple in concept, but hard in execution, and it really just comes down to.....well, don't kill anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T19:13:40-08:00","id":1498723,"title":"","content":"is subsisting on animal blood worthwhille?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"h